WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:07.210
Speaker 1: So the FDA has now authorized for
emergency use while they are still evaluating

00:00:07.210 --> 00:00:15.310
a full approval of the Pfizer covid-19 vaccine,
the Pfizer covid shot has been approved under

00:00:15.310 --> 00:00:17.999
emergency use for 12 to 15 year olds.

00:00:17.999 --> 00:00:25.519
And remember that JNJ and Moderna shots currently
approved 18 plus Pfizer was already 16 plus.

00:00:25.519 --> 00:00:27.880
Now it is 12 plus.

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:35.190
This is a great bit of news because there
are 17 million, 12 to 15 year olds in the

00:00:35.190 --> 00:00:42.579
United States that represents about five,
six percent of the total population.

00:00:42.579 --> 00:00:46.839
And that is a significant chunk, particularly
when we think about students being back in

00:00:46.839 --> 00:00:51.239
school, many already, and almost a certainty
that they will be going back to school in

00:00:51.239 --> 00:00:52.899
person in the fall.

00:00:52.899 --> 00:00:58.969
Being able to make eligible an additional
five or six percent of the total population

00:00:58.969 --> 00:01:00.949
is a really great thing.

00:01:00.949 --> 00:01:03.360
This has been widely tested.

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:09.100
We know that the vaccine is essentially 100
percent effective at preventing serious disease

00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:11.670
and death in 12 to 15 year olds.

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:14.890
It triggers a robust antibody response.

00:01:14.890 --> 00:01:20.430
And there's a recent survey from the Kaiser
Family Foundation Vaccine Monitor which found

00:01:20.430 --> 00:01:27.390
that many parents, even those who have themselves
been vaccinated, are reluctant to vaccinate

00:01:27.390 --> 00:01:33.410
their adolescent kids, sort of in that 12
to 16, 12 to 17 range.

00:01:33.410 --> 00:01:38.660
It's really important that that happens for
several reasons, not the least of which is

00:01:38.660 --> 00:01:44.390
that going back to school without vaccinated
kids just doesn't pass the sniff test.

00:01:44.390 --> 00:01:46.570
It just doesn't make logical sense.

00:01:46.570 --> 00:01:52.110
And we are expecting vaccination for 12 to
15 year olds to start this week.

00:01:52.110 --> 00:01:57.070
Appointments, at least in some states, already
being open to 12 to 15 year olds as soon as

00:01:57.070 --> 00:02:00.190
as soon as tomorrow, as soon as Friday.

00:02:00.190 --> 00:02:08.440
And we are going to see likely, as we saw
with the adult vaccination, an initial surge

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:10.540
and then probably a tapering off.

00:02:10.540 --> 00:02:11.540
And that's fine.

00:02:11.540 --> 00:02:16.390
Just, you know, every time we get new eligibility,
let's get as many people as we can vaccinated.

00:02:16.390 --> 00:02:20.040
And then over the summer, as schools say,
in order to come back on campus, you're going

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:22.180
to need a vaccine.

00:02:22.180 --> 00:02:26.500
You're going to see more and more people in
that age range going get that vaccine.

00:02:26.500 --> 00:02:31.730
States, counties and school districts around
the country, per The New York Times, are trying

00:02:31.730 --> 00:02:37.580
to figure out the most reassuring way to reach
those younger adolescents as well as their

00:02:37.580 --> 00:02:38.580
parents.

00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:44.770
In most states, parents have to consent to
12 to 15 year olds being vaccinated.

00:02:44.770 --> 00:02:49.480
And so it will be not just the 12 to 15 year
olds who need to want to get the shot.

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:54.990
It will also have to be the parents, which
which makes sense in most cases.

00:02:54.990 --> 00:02:59.060
And there are plans to offer the vaccines
not only in schools, but also at pediatricians

00:02:59.060 --> 00:03:01.750
offices, day camps, parks, beaches.

00:03:01.750 --> 00:03:07.620
And we're increasingly hearing about even
some restaurants, in some cases getting involved

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:08.959
in the vaccine effort.

00:03:08.959 --> 00:03:14.310
So, you know, there's no question I've been
seeing on Facebook anecdotally people saying

00:03:14.310 --> 00:03:18.980
my kid is not getting any shot, they're not
getting anything experimental.

00:03:18.980 --> 00:03:19.980
There will be that.

00:03:19.980 --> 00:03:25.910
There is that in every single group that's
going to decline as 12 to 15 year olds start

00:03:25.910 --> 00:03:27.740
to get vaccinated and.

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:34.150
Overwhelmingly start not to get the virus
because the vaccine works so well, certainly

00:03:34.150 --> 00:03:39.930
schools requiring vaccines for in-person attendance
are going to further increase the number of

00:03:39.930 --> 00:03:43.490
parents who will say, well, I wasn't big on
it, but I've got to get these kids out of

00:03:43.490 --> 00:03:44.490
the house.

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:47.720
I mean, quite frankly, it's it's sort of a
silly thing to say to think about it in those

00:03:47.720 --> 00:03:48.720
terms.

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:51.030
But that is going to be a factor as well.

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:57.270
And there are going to be all sorts of mobile
vaccination initiatives and plans to just

00:03:57.270 --> 00:04:01.790
make it as easy as possible for 12 to 15 year
olds to get vaccinated.

00:04:01.790 --> 00:04:07.950
So I continue to say that by Memorial Day,
a lot of these numbers are going to look significantly

00:04:07.950 --> 00:04:08.950
better.

00:04:08.950 --> 00:04:11.150
We expected them to start looking better in
mid-May.

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:12.150
And they are.

00:04:12.150 --> 00:04:13.550
We just went over that.

00:04:13.550 --> 00:04:16.030
Cases are now down 84 percent.

00:04:16.030 --> 00:04:18.559
Deaths are now down 81 percent.

00:04:18.559 --> 00:04:22.009
And there is still you know, I think there's
a couple of things going on.

00:04:22.009 --> 00:04:27.879
There's still a lot of doom and gloom ers
who are only focusing on the negatives.

00:04:27.879 --> 00:04:34.039
And there are negatives, 650 deaths today,
while down 81 percent from the peak, is still

00:04:34.039 --> 00:04:35.240
a lot.

00:04:35.240 --> 00:04:39.870
But in the more vaccinated states, you are
starting to see the daily deaths get down

00:04:39.870 --> 00:04:45.460
to and even below the number of daily deaths
you typically see in a flu season.

00:04:45.460 --> 00:04:51.389
That is very good news, and there is no question
at this point that we are able to vaccinate

00:04:51.389 --> 00:04:52.840
our way out of this.

00:04:52.840 --> 00:04:58.039
So if you have kids in the 12 to 15 age range,
I would love to hear from you.

00:04:58.039 --> 00:05:04.830
How are you thinking of this new emergency
use approval on 12 to 15 if you were vaccinated,

00:05:04.830 --> 00:05:08.729
but you don't plan to have your kids get the
vaccine.

00:05:08.729 --> 00:05:09.729
Let me know why.

00:05:09.729 --> 00:05:11.430
I'd be curious to hear from you.

00:05:11.430 --> 00:05:15.490
And we'll have more about the vaccination
effort on the show's Instagram page.

00:05:15.490 --> 00:05:19.330
Make sure you're following us there at David
Pakman show and make sure you're following

00:05:19.330 --> 00:05:21.610
me on Instagram as well at David Pakman.

00:05:21.610 --> 00:05:22.800
We'll take a quick break.

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:26.520
We will talk about the latest covid lab leak
conspiracy's.

